# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` (version 1.3.1) using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Root Layout Integration
- Modified `app/layout.tsx` to integrate Speed Insights:
  - Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next"`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag, placed after the `<ThemeProvider>` children
  - This placement ensures Speed Insights tracks all page navigation and performance metrics

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows best practices for Next.js 14.2+ with App Router:
- Used `@vercel/speed-insights/next` import (specifically for Next.js 13.5+)
- Added component to root layout for global tracking across all pages
- Preserved existing code structure and functionality
- No breaking changes introduced

## Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully (all 25 routes generated)
- ✅ No TypeScript errors
- ✅ Package dependencies properly installed and locked
- ✅ Speed Insights component properly integrated into the application

## Files Modified

1. `app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component
2. `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
3. `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies

The Speed Insights component will now automatically track Core Web Vitals and page performance metrics when the application is deployed to Vercel.
